{"id": "EUVD-2026-76500", "enisaUuid": "948532e4-298d-354d-9e79-0913c4e3c7bd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: APEI: GHES: fix ARM section length accounting after header\n\nIn ghes_handle_arm_hw_error(), after skipping the cper_sec_proc_arm\nheader with (err + 1), the remaining length was reduced by sizeof(err)\n(pointer size) instead of sizeof(*err) (structure size).\n\nThat overestimates the bytes left for cper_arm_err_info records and can\nlet the parser read past the CPER section when err_info_num is large\nenough relative to error_data_length.\n\nUse sizeof(*err) so the length accounting matches the pointer advance\nand the earlier sizeof(*err) size check.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:20", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ff385e9403e87ae33f65b8c38698d3b1e92cfde", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/452eb28e03015abec6d4bf6488ee567706ade4e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b48b613073c3d652cb1823c15d16f7067cf4cee4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/903308ea40adf0577d82eab69882faf8836326ce"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89588", "GHSA-rcxp-8r6g-r5jm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05c7c8d6-73c9-3c0e-b982-db0ad7451d9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "87880af2d24e62a84ed19943dbdd524f097172f2 <903308ea40adf0577d82eab69882faf8836326ce"}, {"id": "0f3f1e69-cbf5-361d-a73b-37826c966e5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "0fb4a9b7-d264-3477-af32-f984ba1d8d1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "242c652849d979d0133c315a42d9acea0ff88390 <5ff385e9403e87ae33f65b8c38698d3b1e92cfde"}, {"id": "13054ae1-0d50-35a7-9d9b-4a76757c9119", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vend